{
  "id": "mission-01",
  "format": 1,
  "$comment": "T-4.13: mission-01. The greybox-01 combat design is preserved box-for-box — the same two routes, objective, spawn zones, cover and sight lines — and dressed with the T-4.10 kit. Collision remains the proven grey-box geometry while collision-free dirt, road and paving kit tiles give the lanes, start and qalat compound a readable authored surface; later art passes can replace individual structural boxes with matching kit modules without changing mission semantics. T-5.02 adds four low-cover boxes inside the compound (two sandbag runs, two crates): its garrison and the counterattack had nothing inside the walls to take cover behind.",
